    "title": "One man dead, woman critically injured from carbon monoxide poisoning in Gibson County - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ian Young ,\n2 hours ago\nFORT BRANCH, Ind. (WEHT) — One person has died from carbon monoxide poisoning at a home in Gibson County.\nAccording to Gibson County Sheriff Bruce Vanoven, a man is confirmed dead and was found at the bottom of the stairs in a home on the 200 block of South Willard Street. A woman was critically injured from the poisoning and has been taken to a local hospital.\nThis is a developing story.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
